## Role & context

Sidr Launcher, Phase 5. Block L builds the **outbound side** of generation: a pure `PromptContextBuilder`
that assembles an `AiRequest` (the Block-I contract) from the **minimal** context allowed to leave the
device, plus two guard tests that make the privacy posture **fail closed**.

Fork P5-3 (decided): **positive allow-list** — only explicitly listed context may go out, so any future
context addition fails closed until someone deliberately allow-lists it. **Today the assistant input is
essentially the user's typed command — keep it that way.** No device/usage/calendar/location/history
context is assembled. A separate guard mirrors the Phase-4 privacy key-name guard: the API key and raw
prompt never leak into logs / `toString` / the outbound `AiError` surface.

This block is **pure**: everything lands in `:domain` (stdlib + coroutines only). No Android, no Ktor,
no serialization, no `kotlin-reflect`.

