## Acceptance criteria

* `PromptContextBuilder.build(command)` produces a minimal `AiRequest`: one `USER` message = the command
(verbatim), a static context-free system prompt, generation limits, `model == null`; nothing else
assembled.
* The positive allow-list (`OutboundContextPolicy.ALLOWED`) holds only the three vetted categories; the
case-insensitive denylist guard (over static text + field-name inventory, never over user content) is green and would
fail if a forbidden context source or a credential-named field were introduced.
* The secret-leak guard uses Java reflection to enforce sync and proves the outbound surface (`AiRequest` + `AiError` explicit `toString()`) cannot carry the key or raw prompt in any field or `toString`.
* `:domain` stays pure (stdlib + coroutines; no `kotlin-reflect` in `main/`) and vendor-neutral; no new deps;
`IntentMatcher`/`HandleUserCommandUseCase`/`feature/*`/K-M-N artifacts untouched.
* ADR `Block L complete` in `decisions.md` (builder shape + minimal context, positive-allow-list +
fail-closed rationale, denylist-scanned-over-static-text-not-user-content subtlety, reflection-synced guards in test + the "adding an AiRequest field updates OUTBOUND_FIELD_NAMES" rule, explicit `toString` on `AiError`, default system-prompt + token guidance, verification output); `CLAUDE.md` advanced; Block L checked off in `phase-5-plan.md`. **Next = Block M** (router + static fallback + `GenerateReplyUseCase`, consumes K + L).

